<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The morning and evening briefs.

  Install:
    cp ops/com.lms.brief.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.lms.brief.plist

  Run it once by hand before trusting the schedule:
    launchctl kickstart -p gui/$(id -u)/com.lms.brief

  Stop:
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.lms.brief

  ONE JOB, MORNING ONLY. The evening brief needs a second Label and a second
  file, because a plist runs one command; it is not scheduled yet, deliberately.
  Two unread files a day is how a daily brief becomes something Matthew stops
  opening, and until there is any evidence he reads the morning one, adding a
  second is guessing.

  06:30. The mail poll runs at 07:00, AFTER this, which is a stated compromise
  rather than an oversight: putting a network call and twenty inference passes
  in front of the one thing that has to arrive on time would risk delaying it.
  Mail is therefore at most a day late reaching a brief, and the 19:00 poll
  means most of a day is already filed by the time this runs. See
  com.lms.mail.plist.

  DELIVERY IS A FILE IN iCLOUD DRIVE, not Telegram. C2 is unanswered: the app
  is not installed and there is no authorised sender, so there is nothing to
  send to. iCloud is already on his phone, already syncing, and costs nothing
  to set up. When Telegram lands this job changes its command and nothing else.

  A LaunchAgent, not a LaunchDaemon: iCloud Drive is per-user and only exists
  inside a logged-in session. A system daemon would write into a directory that
  never syncs and report success.

  StartCalendarInterval, not StartInterval: if the Mac is asleep at 06:30 the
  job runs at the next opportunity rather than skipping the day. C8 is still
  unanswered, so a machine sitting at a locked login screen is a live scenario.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.lms.brief</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Users/mleca/lms-repo/lms/.venv/bin/python</string>
        <string>/Users/mleca/lms-repo/lms/ops/deliver_brief.py</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/mleca/lms-repo/lms</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <!-- NO LMS_* PATHS HERE. deliver_brief.py reads ops/lms.env itself.
             D-035, and D-045 for the second occurrence. Enforced by
             tests/test_plists.py. -->
        <key>TZ</key>
        <string>America/New_York</string>
        <key>PYTHONUNBUFFERED</key>
        <string>1</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>6</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>

    <!-- One-shot. It writes a file and exits. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/mleca/LMS/logs/brief.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/mleca/LMS/logs/brief.err</string>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
    <key>Nice</key>
    <integer>5</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
